00:25:10.931 --> 00:25:14.100
And I shouldn't have to tell you.


00:25:15.101 --> 00:25:18.271
Do you remember that time
probably 20 years ago?


00:25:18.355 --> 00:25:21.316
You said: "I'm glad
God brought me into this world,


00:25:21.358 --> 00:25:24.110
but I wish it was
from a different father."


00:25:24.152 --> 00:25:26.488
Do you remember that?


00:25:26.529 --> 00:25:30.283
And yet I said nothing,
because I didn't know what to say.


00:25:31.409 --> 00:25:33.411
But it killed me inside.


00:25:34.538 --> 00:25:38.542
And now my little girl is very sick
and I can't fix it.


00:25:40.126 --> 00:25:41.878
So please tell me what to say,


00:25:41.920 --> 00:25:45.048
because I can't have you
hating me like this anymore.


00:25:46.174 --> 00:25:49.427
I love you so very much, Marley.


00:25:51.054 --> 00:25:53.223
Just tell me what to do.


00:25:55.183 --> 00:25:57.394
You just did it.


00:26:05.986 --> 00:26:07.529
Thank you.


00:26:15.704 --> 00:26:17.372
Renee?


00:26:20.792 --> 00:26:22.669
Renee!


00:26:33.972 --> 00:26:37.475
I know you're in here, so I'm just
gonna say what I came here to say,


00:26:37.559 --> 00:26:39.603
which is: I'm sorry.


00:26:39.686 --> 00:26:44.816
It really hurt when you started
distancing yourself, but it's okay.


00:26:44.858 --> 00:26:46.610
I get it.


00:26:46.693 --> 00:26:51.615
A new baby coming
and me-- leaving.


00:26:51.698 --> 00:26:58.496
It's not fair having to be so happy
and so sad at the same time, is it?


00:27:01.583 --> 00:27:04.920
Our friendship is one of the best things
in my life.


00:27:05.003 --> 00:27:08.632
I'm sorry I'm not gonna get
to know that little boy.


00:27:08.715 --> 00:27:12.469
But I know he'll be beautiful.
Just like Cammie.


00:27:14.346 --> 00:27:18.225
Oh, my God, that little girl is amazing.


00:27:22.103 --> 00:27:23.939
So, please, when she gets older


00:27:23.980 --> 00:27:27.317
tell her that I loved her
like she was my own.


00:27:38.411 --> 00:27:39.996
Bye.


00:28:04.771 --> 00:28:07.274
You sure you still want to do this?


00:28:09.568 --> 00:28:10.777
Yeah.


00:28:20.412 --> 00:28:22.581
Wooo! Oh, my God.


00:28:35.427 --> 00:28:37.554
Wooo! Yeah!


00:29:40.951 --> 00:29:42.827
- Same as ever?
- Yeah.


00:29:42.869 --> 00:29:44.246
Really?


00:29:49.125 --> 00:29:51.836
Hey, what are you gonna do
after I'm gone?


00:29:52.879 --> 00:29:54.214
Hum?


00:29:56.049 --> 00:29:59.761
Come on. You got on my case
about not opening up.


00:30:03.181 --> 00:30:06.643
I just don't like thinking about it.


00:30:06.685 --> 00:30:10.647
Julian, I need to know
that you're gonna be okay.


00:30:10.689 --> 00:30:11.773
Oh, my God.


00:30:11.815 --> 00:30:14.150
We should talk about
what we're feeling.


00:30:14.192 --> 00:30:19.072
- Now I've created a monster.
- Yeah, you have.


00:30:21.700 --> 00:30:23.201
So?


00:30:28.582 --> 00:30:29.666
Um,


00:30:30.917 --> 00:30:36.131
so-- this old man
he goes to the doctor,


00:30:36.172 --> 00:30:38.383
and he brings his wife along,


00:30:38.425 --> 00:30:41.386
It's the yearly physical,
so the doctor says:


00:30:41.428 --> 00:30:46.016
"I just need a urine sample,
a blood, a sperm and a stool sample."


00:30:46.057 --> 00:30:50.395
The old man can't hear very well,
so he looks over to his wife


00:30:50.437 --> 00:30:54.107
and asks: "What?
What is he saying?"


00:30:54.149 --> 00:30:57.944
And the wife yells back at him:
"He wants your underwear!"


00:31:03.491 --> 00:31:05.869
My work here is done.


00:31:38.985 --> 00:31:41.655
Ohh.


00:31:51.206 --> 00:31:52.666
Oh.


00:32:40.797 --> 00:32:44.134
So, I have to go back
to New York for a few days, but


00:32:44.217 --> 00:32:46.177
call me if you need anything. Okay?


00:32:46.219 --> 00:32:48.305
Okay, I will.


00:32:49.472 --> 00:32:52.309
-I love you.
<i>-I love you too.</i>


00:32:53.310 --> 00:32:54.853
Bye.


00:33:01.318 --> 00:33:04.779
And this includes
a big opening party?


00:33:06.114 --> 00:33:10.160
Alright, that's what I want.
Great.


00:33:11.411 --> 00:33:13.538
The name is Sarah Walker.


00:33:14.831 --> 00:33:16.291
It's a surprise.


00:33:17.292 --> 00:33:20.879
Okay, thank you very much.
Bye, bye.


00:33:26.718 --> 00:33:31.306
Mom, would you do me a favour
and give this to Sarah for me?


00:33:32.599 --> 00:33:35.977
She's gonna be here in a minute.
You can...


00:33:37.729 --> 00:33:38.897
Oh.


00:33:42.275 --> 00:33:44.527
I'll make sure she gets it.


00:33:49.115 --> 00:33:52.077
And this is for you,


00:34:00.877 --> 00:34:02.837
- It's for me?
- Hm.


00:34:24.067 --> 00:34:25.443
Mom?


00:34:26.778 --> 00:34:28.113
Yeah?


00:34:28.154 --> 00:34:30.532
Will you take care of Stanley for me?


00:34:31.783 --> 00:34:35.662
- I wouldn't have it any other way.
- Check.


00:34:38.915 --> 00:34:40.250
Ah.


00:34:44.087 --> 00:34:45.463
Ah.


00:35:00.103 --> 00:35:02.898
You used to sing me that
to sleep every night.


00:35:25.712 --> 00:35:28.840
Wanna get the ball?
Go get it.


00:35:30.133 --> 00:35:31.801
Get it, buddy.


00:35:35.889 --> 00:35:37.682
Hey.


00:35:37.724 --> 00:35:43.021
I was gonna go for a jog up the hill.
Do you want to come?


00:35:43.104 --> 00:35:48.276
- Sure, You start. I'll catch right up.
- Okay.


00:35:50.237 --> 00:35:56.535
Woo! Yeah. Here we go,
Oh, Oh.


00:35:58.161 --> 00:36:00.455
On second thought,
that's a really big hill.


00:36:01.456 --> 00:36:03.166
Pussy.


00:36:04.334 --> 00:36:06.294
I'm not afraid to admit it.


00:36:08.755 --> 00:36:10.382
Ah.


00:36:14.427 --> 00:36:17.305
When's Julian getting here?


00:36:17.347 --> 00:36:20.350
He had to work late,
so I just left a message.


00:36:22.352 --> 00:36:25.063
Trying to let the poor man sleep.


00:36:31.361 --> 00:36:32.737
- Sarah?
- Hm?


00:36:32.821 --> 00:36:34.322
I'm sorry.


00:36:35.198 --> 00:36:37.826
- What?
- I've been so wrapped up in all this,


00:36:37.909 --> 00:36:42.163
I haven't stopped to ask how
it was affecting all of you guys.


00:36:42.205 --> 00:36:44.833
- Oh, that's...
- Ask how you're doing.


00:36:44.916 --> 00:36:48.211
- It's...
- How are you're doing?


00:36:54.718 --> 00:36:57.095
How are you doing?


00:36:59.598 --> 00:37:01.224
Not so good.


00:37:02.684 --> 00:37:06.062
See?
I didn't know that.


00:37:06.104 --> 00:37:09.733
Why didn't you wish
not to die, huh?


00:37:11.109 --> 00:37:13.695
Hm, something else I wanted more.


00:37:13.737 --> 00:37:19.534
Well, I wish it.
I wish it right now. God?


00:37:19.576 --> 00:37:24.456
Hey? God?
You listening?


00:37:26.249 --> 00:37:29.586
You can't take her away.
Okay?


00:37:31.129 --> 00:37:33.590
I want her to stay here.


00:37:35.091 --> 00:37:39.721
It's not gonna work. You need
an anal probe and a morphine shooter.


00:37:48.271 --> 00:37:51.816
- Are you scared?
- No.


00:37:55.111 --> 00:37:56.738
Not anymore.


00:38:27.602 --> 00:38:29.229
Marley?


00:38:32.482 --> 00:38:33.942
Marley?


00:38:40.031 --> 00:38:41.658
Marley?


00:38:45.161 --> 00:38:46.663
Hey.


00:38:47.956 --> 00:38:50.417
Marley...


00:39:16.443 --> 00:39:17.986
Here you go, sir.


00:39:19.613 --> 00:39:21.197
This is Peter.


00:39:27.495 --> 00:39:29.289
Ahh!


00:40:31.518 --> 00:40:34.229
<i>Hey you, it's me.</i>


00:40:35.647 --> 00:40:40.193
<i>Oh, I didn't think</i>
<i>this was going to be so difficult.</i>


00:40:40.277 --> 00:40:43.905
<i>I thank God you came into my life.</i>
<i>I do.</i>


00:40:43.947 --> 00:40:46.575
<i>Because you showed me</i>
<i>how to be the person</i>


00:40:46.616 --> 00:40:50.161
<i>I always imagined myself to be.</i>


00:40:50.203 --> 00:40:52.330
<i>That's not even</i>
<i>giving you enough credit,</i>


00:40:52.414 --> 00:40:56.209
<i>because until I met you</i>
<i>I had no idea who I could be.</i>


00:40:57.627 --> 00:41:03.800
<i>So-- take care and try</i>
<i>not to fall in love again. Ever.</i>


00:41:03.842 --> 00:41:05.552
<i>Ever again.</i>


00:41:07.554 --> 00:41:09.180
<i>That's kind of a joke.</i>


00:41:10.765 --> 00:41:13.393
- I love you.
- I love you.


00:41:30.243 --> 00:41:35.332
Oh, oh, oh.
I know.


00:42:08.698 --> 00:42:12.202
So, that's my story.


00:42:12.244 --> 00:42:15.622
I had some pretty amazing friends,
didn't I?


00:42:15.664 --> 00:42:20.043
And I include my parents in that group,
even though my whole life I blamed them


00:42:20.126 --> 00:42:22.629
for, well, everything.


00:42:22.671 --> 00:42:28.510
But the truth is: I was afraid.
I was afraid to trust and forgive.


00:42:28.552 --> 00:42:32.389
I was scared I wasn't enough.
But I was.


00:42:49.447 --> 00:42:52.242
To Marley.


00:42:52.284 --> 00:42:54.077
To Marley!


00:43:32.490 --> 00:43:35.076
- Thank you, Marley.
- Thank you, Marley.


00:43:39.497 --> 00:43:40.957
Hi.


00:43:48.506 --> 00:43:49.966
Stanley.


00:44:02.354 --> 00:44:05.065
What I wouldn't give


00:44:05.106 --> 00:44:10.362
to experience just one more time,
to feel that incredible sensation


00:44:12.030 --> 00:44:16.701
when he looked at me
and I felt-- alive.
